Subject: Cantor SJS Compiled Lookahead Repository Candidate Extraction P0 Justification

& [Problem]
  + the selector is executable but every candidate obligation metric and coverage edge must currently be hand-assembled

& [Decision]
  + compile one exact supplied repository-element slice into the unchanged selector request while retaining all semantic claims as supplied declarations

& [Why]
  + this closes auditable lineage and compositional correctness without hiding physical repository reads or semantic inference inside P0
  + authority preflight prevents nonauthority evidence from satisfying mandatory governance
  + exact downstream replay proves the adapter cannot silently change selector semantics

& [Rejected]
  + arbitrary SOP text scanning is rejected because stable semantic identity and coverage cannot be inferred safely from syntax alone
  + embedding or LLM extraction is rejected because provider model calibration and semantic-quality evidence are absent
  + direct prompt injection is rejected because host projection and live A B remain unsigned
